---
// Footer. Reworked 2026-07-22 (website overhaul).
//
// Three things changed and each pays for itself:
//
// 1. The cross-link to adrianmelian.com was a bare URL, so the two sites did not read as a
//    pair. It is now labelled with what is on the other side and which visitor it is for.
//    That is the cheapest half of the two-layer system the whole pass is about.
// 2. Tutorials picked up a footer link, which is the debt the homepage tutorials grid left
//    behind when it was cut.
// 3. GitHub and Report-a-bug are RESTORED. The old comment here held them back because the
//    toolset repo was private pre-launch and they would have 404'd. The repo went public at
//    v1 on 2026-07-20, so the hold expired and the public tracker is the front door the
//    launch posture promised.
//
// Community (YouTube, Instagram) moved down here from the nav in the same pass.
import { LINKS } from '../data/links';
---
<footer>
  <div class="footer__links">
    <a href="/tools/">Pipeline</a>
    <a href="/control-rig/">Control Rig</a>
    <a href="/store/">Store</a>
    <a href="/tutorials/">Tutorials</a>
    <a href="/licensing/">Licensing</a>
    <a href="/changelog/">Changelog</a>
    <a href="/known-issues/">Known issues</a>
    {/* THE SOURCE LINK IS GONE, 2026-09-02. Adrian took the toolset repository private
        at the 2.0 switch - "naw let's go private" - so the URL that stood here is a 404
        for everyone who is not him. Removed rather than repointed: there is no public
        source to link, and a footer link to nothing is worse than no link.

        THE BUG LINK IS A STAND-IN AND NEEDS HIS RULING. The tracker went private with
        the repo. This mailto keeps the door open; it is not a replacement for a public
        tracker, and /known-issues/ still explains a model that assumed one. */}
    <a href={'mailto:contact@fabricator.studio?subject=Bug%20report'}>Report a bug</a>
    <a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a>
    <a href="mailto:adrian@fabricator.studio">Contact</a>
    {LINKS.community.map((c) => (
      <a href={c.href} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{c.label}</a>
    ))}
  </div>
  <p class="footer__pair">
    <a class="footer__pair-link" href="https://adrianmelian.com">Adrian Melian &middot; Technical Director &middot; portfolio and hiring &rarr;</a>
  </p>
  {/* Rewritten 2026-08-31 for the 2.0 posture: the free-toolset claim is dead, and the
      product is the Studio Pipeline (naming in concrete, product-state.md). Sitewide line,
      so it carries identity only, no pitch. */}
  <p class="footer__name">FabricatorStudio. The Studio Pipeline and Armature.</p>
  {/* Third-party credit, site-wide (Adrian, 2026-08-03). The footer rather than a page,
      because the animations appear in videos across several pages and a credit nobody can
      find is not a credit. If this list grows past two or three names it graduates to a
      /credits/ page. */}
  <p class="footer__credit">Animations by <a href="https://www.kubold.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Kubold</a>.</p>
</footer>
<style>
  footer { font-family: var(--font-mono); max-width: 72rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 3rem 1.5rem 4rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--iron-2); text-align: center; }
  .footer__links { display: flex; gap: 1.5rem; flex-wrap: wrap; font-size: 0.9375rem; justify-content: center; }
  .footer__pair { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .footer__pair-link { font-size: 0.9375rem; color: var(--bone); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--iron-3); }
  .footer__pair-link:hover { color: var(--bone); border-color: var(--ember); }
  .footer__name { margin-top: 1.25rem; color: var(--bone-faint); font-size: 0.875rem; }
  .footer__credit { margin-top: 0.5rem; color: var(--bone-faint); font-size: 0.8125rem; }
  .footer__credit a { color: var(--bone-faint); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--iron-3); }
  .footer__credit a:hover { color: var(--bone); border-color: var(--ember); }
</style>
